This instance runs FetchDock, open-source software that downloads media from websites when you ask it to. This policy explains what personal data the instance processes, why, for how long, and who can see it.

FetchDock is designed to collect only the data needed to run the service, with no advertising, tracking, or undisclosed sharing with third parties. FetchDock generated this policy from a list of everything the software stores and sends (kept in sync with the code by automated tests), from this instance's configuration, and from the operator's answers. This generated policy is only published while the instance reports running an unmodified official build (see "Integrity of the software").

## Who is responsible

The controller for your personal data on this instance is {{ a.operator.name ?? missing }}{% if a.operator.address is not null %}, {{ a.operator.address|replace({"\n": ', '}) }}{% endif %}.

{% if a.operator.contactEmail is not null %}
Contact: [{{ a.operator.contactEmail }}](<mailto:{{ a.operator.contactEmail|e('markdown_url')|raw }}>)
{% else %}
Contact: {{ missing }}
{% endif %}

{% if a.operator.dpoContact is not null %}
Data protection officer: {{ a.operator.dpoContact }}
{% endif %}

Because FetchDock is self-hosted, the operator — not the FetchDock project — runs this instance and is responsible for how your data is handled, including any access outside the software. By publishing this policy, the operator adopts it and confirms that your data is not sold or used for advertising.

The FetchDock project only operates the official instance at `api.fetchdock.dev` (and `staging.fetchdock.dev` for testing). Any other FetchDock instance is run independently by its operator — the FetchDock project does not operate it and receives no personal data from it, unless an administrator shares a problem report with the FetchDock maintainers for support (see "Problem reports").

## Legal basis

- **Providing the service (downloads, settings and device sync):** {% if a.legalBasis == 'contract' %}performance of a contract to provide the download service you signed up for (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).{% elseif a.legalBasis == 'legitimate_interest' %}the operator's legitimate interest in providing the download service to the people they admitted (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object to this processing (see "Your rights"), though the download service cannot work without processing the data required for a download.{% else %}{{ missing }}{% endif %}

- **Logs and security:** the operator's legitimate interest in keeping the service secure and working reliably (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
- **Problem reports** (when enabled on this instance): your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Nothing is sent unless you choose to send a report, and you can withdraw your consent at any time by withdrawing the report. Whether problem reports are enabled is published in this instance's configuration at `/.well-known/browser-extension`.

You are not legally required to provide personal data. However, signing in and providing a URL (mandatory) are necessary to use the download service, and some websites also require your cookies, user agent or referring page (optional by default, mandatory for certain sites) in order to download media — without the data needed for a download, the service cannot perform it.

